## Wf-378..392 ultracode decisions (2026-09-30)

**Appended per Wf-393-A3 docs-only sync** — captures 5 NEW architectural decisions
from the Wf-380 / Wf-385 / Wf-386 / Wf-388 / Wf-390 ultracode CPU-only waves
(2026-09-30). Per `party-twenty-spirit` §3.5 + AGENTS.md §5.2: every numeric claim
traces to a JSON / report path; MEASURED-vs-PROJECTED tag preserved. Standing
directives §5.1 (Standing GPU authorization) + §5.3 (no paper work) + §5.4
(Tier-2 + NO wet-lab planning per 2026-09-29/30 user directive) + §10 (wetlab
deprecation FAQ) re-confirmed.

### D-Wf-380 ✅ CFM SCAFFOLD + 14 CFM CLI flags + 3 DMPNN CLI flags wired (default ON)

- **Decision:** Author 10 NEW CFM innovation SCAFFOLD modules (~1055 LOC) at
  `molmetal/adapters/flow_matching_lipman/{edm_preconditioning,optimal_transport_v2_solver,
  stable_vm,so3_average,triton_mini_batch_ot,shortcut_distillation_wf380,
  consistency_regularization_wf380,flowmol_unified,log_normal_t,lr_warmup}.py` + wire
  14 NEW CFM CLI flags + 7 `--no-X` negation flags + 1-line banner into
  `molmetal/scripts/train_cfm_yuelbond_wasserstein.py` (parse_args lines 1487-1740)
  + 3 NEW DMPNN CLI flags + 3 `--no-X` negation flags + 1-line banner into
  `molmetal/scripts/train_dmpnn_multitask_wasserstein.py` (parse_args lines 3001-3083).
- **Default semantics:** `--no-X` negation pattern means the X capability is **default ON**
  (e.g. `--use-yuelbond` default True + `--no-yuelbond` negation). Matches existing
  pre-Wf-380 trainer flag conventions (e.g. `--use-yuelbond` at line 1020,
  `--closure-bounded` at line 1029).
- **Honest framing caveat:** the 14 CFM + 3 DMPNN CLI flags are **SCAFFOLD-only**
  observability / dispatcher patterns — they are declared in `parse_args` + printed in
  the Wf-380 banner code, but ZERO loss / sampling / dispatch wire-in to the live
  training computation at the read-site (per Wf-385-A1 audit: 0/17 flags have an
  actual SCAFFOLD call in the main training loop; 0/17 flags have the SCAFFOLD module
  imported by the trainer; 17/17 are FLAG_ONLY). The MEASURED wire-in closes
  incrementally via Wf-388 (m7 Diversity 6/6 flags + m4 SA 2/2 flags) + Wf-389 +
  Wf-390; remaining SCAFFOLD-loss wire-in deferred to Wf-381+ per Wf-385-A1 §6
  closure path (~280 LOC + ~12 tests PROJECTED on Blackwell sm_120 + GPU retrain
  USER_OK-gated per AGENTS.md §5.1).
- **Evidence:** `TODO/completed/380a1_deep_integration_scaffolds.md` (10 SCAFFOLD
  modules + 41/41 NEW tests PASS) + `TODO/completed/380b1_index_sync.md` (trainer
  integration details + 14+3 flag listing) + `TODO/completed/380_final_synthesis.md`
  (~700 LOC §0-§9 comprehensive synthesis) + `TODO/completed/385a1_wf380_cli_flag_audit.md`
  (the SCAFFOLD-only honest-negative audit). Pre-flight v3 89/2/3/94 PRESERVED at
  Wf-380-B1 timestamp.
- **Approved by:** Wf-380-B1 + Wf-385-A1 + Wf-393-A3 docs sync (user directive
  2026-09-30 verbatim *"如果是同一个问题一直没修好的话得做调研+review尝试更深层
  的修复"* — Wf-385 is the deeper-fix that audits + adds the wire-in gate; SCAFFOLD
  authoring is the surface fix).
- **Reopens if:** MEASURED wire-in of remaining SCAFFOLD flags to main training loop
  via Wf-381+ (~280 LOC across 17 read-sites + ~12 tests PROJECTED). Then revisit
  flag default semantics if MEASURED end-to-end lift projects a threshold gap.

### D-Wf-385 ✅ Pre-flight gate `p3_wf385_scaffold_loss_wire_in_verified` added

- **Decision:** Ship a NEW pre-flight gate `p3_wf385_scaffold_loss_wire_in_verified`
  that catches SCAFFOLD-only failures at pre-flight time, complementing (NOT
  replacing) the SCAFFOLD-loss actual wire-in.
- **Mechanism:** Script at `molmetal/scripts/wf385a3_scaffold_wire_in_gate.py`
  ~280 LOC reads the Wf-385-A1 audit JSON
  (`molmetal/reports/wf385a3_scaffold_wire_in/gate_result.json`) + verifies that for
  every Wf-380 SCAFFOLD CLI flag, there is at least one read-site in the trainer
  source code that ACTUALLY consumes the flag's value in a loss / sampling /
  dispatch path. If a flag is FLAG_ONLY (no read-site beyond parse_args), the
  gate flags `WIRE_IN_MISSING` for that flag. Gate registered as `'all'-only` (NOT
  in `frontier` / `chemprop_v2_v3` / `cfm` per-pipeline sub-counts); gate count
  auto-recompute per Wf-345-B3 keeps `EXPECTED_GATE_COUNTS["all"] = 94`
  PRESERVED.
- **Test suite:** `molmetal/tests/test_wf385a3_scaffold_wire_in_gate.py` ~332 LOC,
  20 NEW tests across 5 test classes, all PASS at Wf-385-A3 timestamp.
- **Evidence:** `TODO/completed/385a3_scaffold_wire_in_gate.md` (gate definition
  + 20-test plan + MEASURED gate_result.json) + `TODO/completed/385a1_wf380_cli_flag_audit.md`
  (the upstream audit that surfaced the gate need) + `TODO/completed/385_final_synthesis.md`
  (~580 LOC §0-§9 comprehensive synthesis v28).
- **Approved by:** Wf-385-A3 + Wf-393-A3 docs sync (user directive 2026-09-30
  verbatim *"如果是同一个问题一直没修好的话得做调研+review尝试更深层的修复"* —
  gate is the deeper-fix substrate that catches SCAFFOLD-only at pre-flight time
  rather than after-the-fact audit).
- **Reopens if:** SCAFFOLD-loss MEASURED wire-in completes via Wf-381+; then gate
  contract shifts from "audit" to "verify-actually-active" — reopens if SCAFFOLD
  surface expands (e.g. Wf-400+ ships 17 more flags).

### D-Wf-386 ✅ Atomic write protocol adopted (AGENTS.md §5.6)

- **Decision:** Adopt the atomic write protocol via 3 NEW helper functions at
  `molmetal/scripts/wf386a3_atomic_write.py` (~366 LOC):
  1. `atomic_write_file(path, content, *, encoding="utf-8", fsync=True)` —
     atomic temp-file + rename with per-path lock + fsync for crash safety
  2. `safe_overwrite_check(path, new_content, *, min_lines=50,
     diff_threshold=0.5, raise_on_risk=False)` — line-set Jaccard distance +
     threshold guard against destructive overwrite of unrelated content
  3. `detect_truncation(agent_output, *, expected_min_length=200)` —
     closing-token heuristic + length check to detect truncated agent outputs
     before they ship as closeouts
- **Process adoption:** AGENTS.md §5.6 NEW MANDATE (added per Wf-386-B1) — every
  closeout write MUST use `atomic_write_file`; overwrite-write MUST run
  `safe_overwrite_check`; agent verification MUST run `detect_truncation`.
  Complement to the agent-prompt governance rule added per Wf-384 §5.5 (post-wave
  `ls -la` evidence mandate). Belt-and-braces defence at TWO levels: agent-prompt
  governance (Wf-384) + I/O substrate (Wf-386).
- **Trigger:** recurring "verification reliability + write overwriting" pattern
  surfaced across Wf-371 / Wf-373 / Wf-377 / Wf-378 / Wf-384 — root-caused via
  Wf-386-A1 (Wf-384-A3 overwrite audit) + Wf-386-A2 (Wf-378-A3 wrong-verdict
  root cause).
- **Test suite:** `molmetal/tests/test_wf386a3_atomic_write.py` ~332 LOC,
  27-case test suite PASS at Wf-386-A3 timestamp.
- **Evidence:** `TODO/completed/386a3_atomic_write_protocol.md` (full protocol
  definition + §2-§5 implementation + §6 adoption sequence) + `docs/ATOMIC_WRITE_PROTOCOL.md`
  ~290 LOC (operator-facing docs) + `AGENTS.md` §5.6 (MANDATE cross-ref).
- **Approved by:** Wf-386-A3 + Wf-393-A3 docs sync (user directive 2026-09-30
  verbatim *"如果是同一个问题一直没修好的话得做调研+review尝试更深层的修复"* —
  atomic write protocol is the deeper-fix that converts the recurring verification
  + write pattern into a substrate-level defence).

